WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.100
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.801
We're hanging out with
Mark Wahlberg right here.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ah, one of our favorites.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.567
And we always like
to do something fun

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:09.734
when you're on the show.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.133
You're a good sport.
Thank you for doing that.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.968
Since we're both competitive,
I thought we could compete

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.467
in a series of challenges --

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:17.067
challenges we can get done
in just 30 seconds.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:20.167
It's time for "30 Seconds To..."
Here we go.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:22.934
♪ 30 Seconds To... ♪

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.100
-so we have 30 seconds to...
blank.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.467
That's the way the game works.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.901
For this first challenge,
we'll have 30 seconds

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:33.067
to fill our cups with as many
green Skittles as we can.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.834
Thank you.
Whoever gets the most, wins.

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.601
So just only green Skittles.

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:40.167
I feel like you have more green
in your bowl.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.167
Already this feels rigged to me.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:44.167
-It's just
a Boston Celtic thing.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:45.667
It looks that way,
but it's not, really.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.267
-Yeah. It's a Boston thing.
Alright.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:50.634
We have 30 seconds on the clock.
Ready, set, go.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:53.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:58.767
♪♪

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.067
-Oh, my God. This is not good.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:01.734
-Oh, no.
I put an orange one in there.

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.200
-It's going like a -- Yeah,
now you got to clean it out.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.601
-I messed up. I messed up.
-That's --

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:07.067
-Yeah, that's -- That's where --
Quest, you're making me nervous!

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.934
-Oh, no.
-How many seconds?

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:12.100
Oh. I got a red one there.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.367
Eight.

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:16.467
Audience: 8, 7, 6...

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:19.033
-Ah. God.
-...5, 4, 3...

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.467
2, 1!

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.834
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.167
-I got a couple of others
in there.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.767
-What do we -- How do we know?
We have to count them out?

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.400
-I just figured if I went back
and just started

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.234
taking them out,
you lost so much time, man.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:32.701
-Oh, wait. So you already have
other colors.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.667
So I totally win.
I win that one, right?

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.067
-You got that one.
-Alright. I got that one.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.067
Cool. Cheers. Right?
-It looks like edamame.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.400
-Right? Yeah, hang on.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.701
[ Applause ]

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.167
Alright, who went -- Wait.
You're getting them out

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.834
as you're pulling them out
and counting them?

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.801
Alright. I have this many.
One, two...

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:48.934
I got, like, 15 or something.
What do you got?

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.801
-I got more than 15.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.367
-You do? Oh, yeah.
You crushed me.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:53.834
Mark Wahlberg wins that one.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.267
-I -- I didn't have
the right amount.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.601
[ Bell dinging ]

00:01:56.601 --> 00:01:58.000
-You win round one.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.200
-You like to win
and then say you lost.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.434
-No -- Yeah, exactly.
-I see the game.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.000
[ Cup bounces ]
-Alright, here we go.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.701
For this next challenge --
For this next challenge,

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.033
we'll have 30 seconds
to see who can get the most

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.434
ping-pong balls
into a red Solo cup.

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:11.601
-Oh, gosh.
-I think --

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.300
I don't even know if I --
-Beer pong.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.067
-I don't even know
if I can get one in.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.934
-I think you play this game
for a living.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.300
Professional beer ponger.
-Actually, I am.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.334
Yeah, I get paid on the show
to play beer pong.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.300
It's a great gig, man.
It's a great gig.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.000
Alright. Let's get 30 seconds
on the clock.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.701
-For real, I don't think
I'm going to make one.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:29.667
-Alright, good luck.
Here we go.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.067
Go.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:33.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:34.701
-Oh, [bleep].
I'm not even in the area.

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:37.033
I don't even have the right --
No, I'm not even close.

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:40.167
-I -- I -- Now I'm drifting.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:41.534
I haven't hit the cup yet.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:43.334
-I'm throwing two at a time now.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:46.100
♪♪

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.767
I got one. I got one!

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:52.834
♪♪

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.934
-I got one in.
-Yeah, I got one, too.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:58.601
Oh, I got two!
-I got it.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.100
-Ooh.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.467
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.868
This is amaz--
-I got a lot of rim.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.701
-Amazing skill. Yeah.
I got --

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:10.033
-Oh, no, I got --
-How many did you get?

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:11.534
-I got two.

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:14.200
-That's interesting,
because I got three!

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:17.801
[ Bell dinging ]

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.100
We had a good strategy
right there.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.567
-Yeah, yeah.
-Alright, we're tied up.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.200
We're tied up and we're down
to the final challenge, okay?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.834
-He's gonna have to pick up
all the balls.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.334
-And this is the --
-Sorry about that. I apologize.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.934
-No, this is -- this is fun.
This is "The Tonight Show."

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.834
It's what it should be.
Ping-pong balls everywhere.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:33.234
This final challenge,
we have 30 seconds to stick

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:36.667
as many Post-it notes
to our bodies as we can.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.467
-Oh, boy.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:42.234
-Whoever sticks the most Post-it
notes on their body wins.

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:43.400
You ready for this?

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.834
-They took your --
half your stack.

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:47.901
-Yeah. Yeah, I do -- I feel
like my stack is little, yeah.

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:50.267
Thanks. Appreciate it.
Thank you very much.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:53.667
Okay, now I have more.
Now this feels weird.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.067
Oh, you have some there.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.834
Alright.
Alright, ready for this?

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.033
Can we do that? Is that okay?

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.868
Alright. Let's get 30 seconds
on the clock.

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.534
On your mark. Get set. Go.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:12.200
♪♪

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.734
I went too thick.
I went too thick.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:19.968
It's harder than you think!

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.667
Your -- It sticks to your face
pretty well.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.200
-You got to do multiple.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.467
♪♪

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:27.167
-There you go.

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:30.601
♪♪

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:32.467
-Oh, I'm losing them.

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.100
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:38.100
-There's not even a comparison.
-I got --

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.901
-I think we all know who
the winner is right there,

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:41.400
the one and only.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.601
[ Bell dinging ]

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:46.467
Mark Wahlberg! The champ!

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:48.567
Guys, his movie "Me Time"

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:52.167
is available on Netflix
August 26th with Kevin Hart.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.000
Billy Porter joins us
after the break.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.300
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back.

